comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T08:44:27.650Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: all-status searches covered merge guidance, discarded values, pm merge report, durable receipts, and post-merge settlement. Closed pm-rh98vo created durable conflict reports; open pm-lwmstb owns receipt settlement after merge. Neither owns the missing recovery pointer at conflict time. GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/889"
  "2026-08-04T09:18:26.565Z","harness:codex","Graph correction 2026-08-04: removed the initial blocked_by edge to pm-lwmstb after reviewing both scopes. Durable receipt settlement is adjacent downstream work, but it does not prevent conflict-time recovery guidance from exposing the existing report. The remaining implements and discovered_from edges state the evidence-backed lineage without inventing execution order."
  "2026-08-04T11:47:38.550Z","harness:codex","Evidence: unresolved merge guidance now always points to pm merge report and, when present, includes privacy-safe receipt_id/item_id correlation without exposing discarded values. Linked merge safety/receipt tests passed; full coverage and lint gates passed."
  "2026-08-04T11:52:04.240Z","harness:codex","Review handoff: PR #893 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/893 at initial head 6c31a5f18 packages this item with the related SDK/CLI governance tranche."
  "2026-08-04T12:23:25.965Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: PR #893 exact head a8ea2b426 passed every hosted check, including static, 4 coverage shards plus coverage gate, typecheck, compatibility, smokes, Windows, benchmarks, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, DeepScan, CodeFactor, Codecov, and CodSpeed. Sourcery's actionable flag-normalization thread was implemented/replied/resolved; all bot comments/reviews were reacted to and acknowledged. CodeRabbit was quota-limited and Greptile supplied no response within the review window."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
